    Plan the weight-claim merge into one pending claim
    
    The merge registers the claims' end-value slots before any challenge, batches them with one challenge, takes the sumcheck point over the matrix column bits and records the masked end value, whose slot may not reuse a claim's slot. The pending claim consumes the point lowest column bit first and carries the mask factor as the index-mask coefficient. The runtime reduced-witness plan is built from settled plan tables with contiguous offsets, checked entry counts and every point set.
    
    This is partial progress: the first-chain message and the read binding are the next step.

